                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "To put this succinctly - this is a randomly generated puzzle game where they've expected random generation to make for an infinitely replayable game. The base concepts and executions are so poor, however, that it amounts to an infinite void of boring nonsense. Random generation is the main problem here - in that it robs any identity or character the game might've had, and offers the abysmal mechanics nothing to hide behind. Calling this \"two\" games is only true insofar as there are two executeables, the differences seem to be so insignificant as to explain why they're packaged together. Really, don't bother.",
